  "query_preview": "through 2 PM Saturday for Kent and Sussex, DE. Tide \nlevels are high enough though on the New Jersey side of the Bay \nto result in minor tidal flooding, even with the wind pushing\nwater away from the NJ Delaware Bay coastline. Confidence is \nhigh enough to warrant an extension to the Coastal Flood \nAdvisory for Cumberland through 1 PM Saturday\n\nAs mentioned above, more north/northeasterly winds will limit \nthe tidal flooding threat for the Chesapeake Bay. Some spotty \nminor tidal flooding is anticipated at Claiborne, but nothing \nhigher than that at this time. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Dangerous rip currents and high surf are \nexpected at the Jersey Shore and Delaware Beaches through\nSaturday. Beach erosion is likely and breaching of sand dunes \nis possible.\n\nA nor'easter off our coast will bring strong north to northeast\nwinds and high seas for our marine zones. Breaking waves within\nthe surf zone of 6 to 12 feet are expected through Saturday. \nDangerous rip currents will accompany the high surf, making it \nextremely dangerous to enter the water at any time through \nSaturday. The high surf and strong winds will likely result in \nareas of beach erosion across the Jersey Shore and Delaware \nBeaches. Large breaking waves in the surf zone and high water \nlevels may result in breaching of sand dunes.\n\nThe High Risk for life threatening rip currents remains in \neffect through Saturday for all beaches. A High Surf Advisory is\nin effect for all beaches through Saturday as well.",
